Hi everyone! <div><br></div><div>A few months ago when I ran my code, I obtained better fit indices and never once experienced the following error code: </div><div><br></div><div><font color="#ff0000">lavaan WARNING: using a single label per parameter in a multiple group
	 setting implies imposing equality constraints across all the groups;
	 If this is not intended, either remove the label(s), or use a vector
	 of labels (one for each group);
	 See the Multiple groups section in the man page of model.syntax.lavaan WARNING: some estimated ov variances are negativelavaan WARNING: some estimated lv variances are negative</font><br></div><div><font color="#ff0000"><br></font></div><div><font color="#000000">Now that I am revisiting my analyses - that message popped up and my fit indices tanked (CFI now = .875; CFI back then = .91)  </font></div><div><font color="#000000"><br></font></div><div><font color="#000000"><b>Below is my model code. </b></font></div><div><font color="#000000"><b>My question is, has anyone experienced this? By chance is there a solution to this error message that may be worsening my fit indices?</b></font></div><div><font color="#000000"><b><br></b></font></div><div><div>NeighInflu=~1.0*PhysDis</div><div>NegPerCh=~1.0*Impul</div><div>NegPerCh=~1.0*Unemo</div><div>PeerInf=~1.0*PerDel</div><div><br></div><div><div>NeighInflu=~NeighInflu_Alc*Alc<br></div></div><div>NegPerCh=~NegPerCh_Alc*Alc</div><div>PeerInf=~PeerInf_Alc*Alc</div><div><br></div><div>Marij~Alc_Marij*Alc</div><div><br></div><div>NeighInflu~~VAR_NeighInflu*NeighInflu      </div><div>PhysDis~~VAR_PhysDis*PhysDis              </div><div><br></div><div>NegPerCh~~VAR_NegPerCh*NegPerCh            </div><div>Impul~~VAR_Impul*Impul                    </div><div>Unemo~~VAR_Unemo*Unemo                      </div><div><br></div><div>PeerInf~~VAR_PeerInf*PeerInf                </div><div>PerDel~~VAR_PerDel*PerDel              </div><div><br></div><div>Alc~~Var_Alc*Alc                     </div><div>Marij~~VAR_Marij*Marij               </div><div><br></div><div>NeighInflu~~NegPerCh<br></div><div>NeighInflu~~PeerInf</div><div>NegPerCh~~PeerInf</div><div><br></div><div>Marij~~Age<br></div><div>Alc~~Age</div><div><br></div><div>PhysDis~1;</div><div>Impul~1;</div><div>Unemo~1;</div><div>Alc~1;</div><div>Marij~1;</div><div>&#39;</div><div>mymodel.6.fit&lt;- cfa(mymodel.6,</div><div>                     data=project, </div><div>                    group = &quot;Race&quot;,</div><div>                    fixed.x=FALSE, estimator = &quot;MLR&quot;, missing=&quot;FIML&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>summary(mymodel.6.fit,</div><div>        rsquare=TRUE,</div><div>        standardized=TRUE,</div><div>        fit.measures=TRUE) </div><div><br></div><div>fitmeasures(mymodel.6.fit, c(&quot;cfi&quot;, &quot;rmsea&quot;,&quot;tli&quot;,estimator=&quot;MLR&quot;))</div></div><div><br></div><div>Best, </div><div>Sarah </div>
